WEBVTT

00:00:08,980 --> 00:00:13,780
I have heard that increased, you know,

00:00:13,780 --> 00:00:21,650
sinophils means I have allergies, is that true?

00:00:21,650 --> 00:00:23,050
Possibly, yeah.

00:00:23,050 --> 00:00:26,450
So, yes, sinophils are a type of white blood cell.

00:00:26,450 --> 00:00:29,250
When you get your CBC done,

00:00:29,250 --> 00:00:31,450
you want to get a CBC with differential.

00:00:31,450 --> 00:00:34,450
Now, most clinics are never going to run a CBC

00:00:34,450 --> 00:00:35,950
without running a differential.

00:00:35,950 --> 00:00:38,650
I mean, a differential means you're differentiating

00:00:38,650 --> 00:00:41,950
between the types of white blood cells that we're measuring.

00:00:42,350 --> 00:00:47,550
So, now, I have seen, especially in the hospital setting,

00:00:47,550 --> 00:00:51,550
where they'll, somebody goes into the emergency route

00:00:51,550 --> 00:00:54,850
and they just run us in a simple,

00:00:54,850 --> 00:00:58,650
you know, some simple metabolic panel.

00:00:58,650 --> 00:00:59,650
It's like, good mistakes.

00:00:59,650 --> 00:01:02,350
And then they charge a person's insurance, you know,

00:01:02,350 --> 00:01:05,350
$1,000 for this $5 test.

00:01:05,350 --> 00:01:07,050
It's absolutely ridiculous.

00:01:07,050 --> 00:01:08,350
And you don't run a differential.

00:01:08,350 --> 00:01:11,250
It's absolutely no sense if you're going to do a CBC

00:01:11,250 --> 00:01:13,350
without running a differential.

00:01:13,350 --> 00:01:17,250
So, the differential splits out the white blood cells

00:01:17,250 --> 00:01:20,050
into, you know, it's major components.

00:01:20,050 --> 00:01:22,450
There's, you could split it out much deeper

00:01:22,450 --> 00:01:25,350
and do a whole lymphocyte panel.

00:01:25,350 --> 00:01:28,250
But, it splits it out into its major components.

00:01:28,250 --> 00:01:30,850
What's, how many lymphocytes actually?

00:01:30,850 --> 00:01:32,850
Absolute is called the,

00:01:32,850 --> 00:01:35,650
the numbers that they count in the slide

00:01:35,650 --> 00:01:38,250
that they're looking at, and then percentage.

00:01:38,250 --> 00:01:41,150
So, you typically, the differential you have

00:01:41,250 --> 00:01:43,450
lymphocytes, neutrophils, basophils,

00:01:43,450 --> 00:01:45,950
eosinophils, monocytes.

00:01:45,950 --> 00:01:50,750
And then it'll give a absolute value and a percentage value.

00:01:50,750 --> 00:01:54,250
So, if you have an increased absolute value

00:01:54,250 --> 00:01:56,550
and an increased percentage value

00:01:56,550 --> 00:01:57,950
of one of those things,

00:01:57,950 --> 00:02:02,050
it gives you clues to why the white blood cell count

00:02:02,050 --> 00:02:03,150
may be elevated.

00:02:03,150 --> 00:02:04,950
You could even have a normal white blood cell count.

00:02:04,950 --> 00:02:07,750
You could have an abnormal differential.

00:02:07,750 --> 00:02:10,950
So, on these, we've discussed the differentials

00:02:10,950 --> 00:02:14,050
on the white blood cells with neutrophils before.

00:02:14,050 --> 00:02:16,450
Typically, if you have an elevated neutrophil,

00:02:16,450 --> 00:02:19,250
it may be significant that you have a bacterial infection.

00:02:19,250 --> 00:02:21,250
Typically, if you have an elevated lymphocyte,

00:02:21,250 --> 00:02:23,650
it may be more critical

00:02:23,650 --> 00:02:25,850
that you have a viral infection.

00:02:25,850 --> 00:02:29,150
If you have an elevated eosinophil,

00:02:29,150 --> 00:02:30,950
does that mean that you have an allergy?

00:02:30,950 --> 00:02:33,850
It can be, that's one of the things that it can be.

00:02:33,850 --> 00:02:37,050
So, food allergies, environmental allergies,

00:02:37,050 --> 00:02:40,750
you know, a person that has really bad environmental allergies

00:02:40,750 --> 00:02:42,050
that say pollen allergies

00:02:42,050 --> 00:02:45,450
can have an elevated eosinophil at that time of the year.

00:02:45,450 --> 00:02:47,950
So, that can be significant,

00:02:47,950 --> 00:02:52,450
but also intestinal parasites can increase eosinophils.

00:02:54,250 --> 00:02:56,650
And then people with allergic type conditions

00:02:56,650 --> 00:02:59,550
like asthma can have an elevated eosinophil.

00:02:59,550 --> 00:03:04,550
So, just like any of the other differential components,

00:03:06,950 --> 00:03:09,150
it's not a perfect science.

00:03:09,150 --> 00:03:10,950
It's like, oh, if you have this, then you have this.

00:03:10,950 --> 00:03:13,850
You know, you have to correlate it with other things.

00:03:13,850 --> 00:03:15,750
Let's say the person, you know,

00:03:15,750 --> 00:03:19,550
we did a stool sample test and they have no intestinal parasites

00:03:19,550 --> 00:03:22,050
and no symptoms of intestinal parasites,

00:03:22,050 --> 00:03:26,450
but they, you know, they have signs and symptoms of allergies

00:03:26,450 --> 00:03:28,550
that you might correlate it with.

00:03:28,550 --> 00:03:30,850
That's probably what it's coming from.

00:03:30,850 --> 00:03:32,750
And then that would certainly spark you too.

00:03:32,750 --> 00:03:34,350
Maybe we should run a food panel

00:03:34,350 --> 00:03:36,550
or maybe we should do this or whatever.

00:03:36,550 --> 00:03:40,150
But even with most food sensitivities

00:03:40,150 --> 00:03:44,650
and such, you don't see acute uprise in eosinophils

00:03:44,650 --> 00:03:46,550
unless it's an acute condition.

00:03:46,550 --> 00:03:48,750
And remember, you're drawing this blood

00:03:48,750 --> 00:03:52,350
at just one specific time of the day

00:03:52,350 --> 00:03:54,350
that you're drawing to, you know,

00:03:54,350 --> 00:03:58,150
this pile of blood out of a person's arm.

00:03:58,150 --> 00:04:00,850
So, it really depends on what's going on

00:04:00,850 --> 00:04:03,250
specifically at that time with that individual.

00:04:03,250 --> 00:04:07,550
So, it's not elevated in eosinophils.uncommon,

00:04:07,550 --> 00:04:10,050
but it's certainly not common.

00:04:10,050 --> 00:04:12,050
And so, you would look,

00:04:12,050 --> 00:04:15,250
you just, it was spark you to look for the reason why.

00:04:15,250 --> 00:04:17,750
But the biggest reasons why it would be a intestinal parasites,

00:04:17,750 --> 00:04:21,650
food sensitivities, environmental sensitivities,

00:04:21,650 --> 00:04:24,650
there's some sort of allergic condition going on.

00:04:24,650 --> 00:04:28,650
Maybe even a hypersense type of mass cell response

00:04:28,650 --> 00:04:30,450
at that particular time.

00:04:30,450 --> 00:04:32,250
Asba, something like that,

00:04:32,250 --> 00:04:34,750
you'd be looking at those possibilities.

